          {
            "id": "les_da_02",
            "section_id": "sec_da_01",
            "title": "1.2 SQL Business Case: Retention & Churn Analytics",
            "type": "article",
            "content": "### Analyzing Customer Churn with SQL Window Functions\n\nCohort retention analysis is one of the most requested deliverables for professional data analysts.\n\n```sql\nWITH monthly_activity AS (\n  SELECT \n    user_id,\n    DATE_TRUNC('month', activity_date) AS activity_month,\n    FIRST_VALUE(DATE_TRUNC('month', activity_date)) OVER (\n      PARTITION BY user_id ORDER BY activity_date\n    ) AS cohort_month\n  FROM user_events\n)\nSELECT \n  cohort_month,\n  activity_month,\n  COUNT(DISTINCT user_id) AS active_users\nFROM monthly_activity\nGROUP BY 1, 2\nORDER BY 1, 2;\n```\n\nThis pattern allows executive stakeholders to track subscriber lifetime value and optimize retention funnels.",
            "duration_seconds": 380,
            "position": 2,
            "is_free_preview": true,
            "is_completed": false
          }
        ]
      }
